// Can a full-screen program show the terminal's cursor where the next
// character will go?
//
// Hypothesis DIS-ZYE-004 (HALLAZGOS.md). On the day it was filed it could not:
// `>>|` hides the cursor on entry and nothing in the language showed it. This
// program is what an editor does on its first frame: draw a line, then wait for
// a key with the caret after the text. Since D-16 (2026-11-23) the line that
// shows the cursor is `>>~ (row, col)` with nothing to print.
>>| {
    >>!
    >>~ (1, 1) > "hello"
    >>~ (1, 6)          // show the terminal's cursor at row 1, column 6
    <<| _k
}
